  "goodToKnow": "Protestantisch means Protestant; in everyday German, people say evangelisch: Ich bin evangelisch. The Reformation began in 1517 when Martin Luther published his 95 theses in Wittenberg; the name comes from the 1529 protest of Lutheran princes at the Diet of Speyer. Northern and eastern Germany are historically Protestant, the south and west more Catholic. Max Weber linked die protestantische Ethik to capitalism."
